; Game clock text: 6 characters
;
; The time of day as ASCII, printed at column 25 of row 19 each frame (#R$89AD):
; hours (blank or "1", then a digit), ":", minutes (two digits), and the letter
; "a" or "p". Starts as " 7:00a" (copied from #R$8585 by #R$88AE). The minutes
; advance each time the frame counter #R$85CB wraps to 0 (every 256 passes of
; the game loop; observed). The hour goes 12 to 1 and switches "a" to "p" there;
; the game ends and restarts (#R$87CA) when the clock reaches 13:00 with the
; letter "p" (observed with "12:59p"). Poked values: " 9:59a" gives "10:00a",
; "12:59a" gives " 1:00p".
@label=ClockText
t$857F DEFM " 7:00a"
